---
import LegalLayout from '../components/ui/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<LegalLayout title="Data deletion" description="How to delete your Creators Club data or disconnect Instagram and YouTube." updated="13 November 2026">
  <h2>Disconnect Instagram or YouTube</h2>
  <p>Sign in at <a href={SITE.appUrl}>app.creatorsclub.co.in</a>, open <strong>Platforms</strong> (or Platforms in the mobile app) and disconnect the account. Its access tokens are erased and its automations stop immediately.</p>

  <h2>Remove Creators Club in Meta or Google settings</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Facebook: Settings &amp; privacy → Settings → Business integrations → remove Creators Club.</li>
    <li>Instagram: Settings → Website permissions → Apps and websites → remove Creators Club.</li>
    <li>Google: myaccount.google.com/permissions → remove Creators Club.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Requests from Meta</h2>
  <p>When you remove the app on Facebook or Instagram, Meta notifies us automatically. We delete the data we received for that account and give Meta a confirmation code you can use to check the status of your request.</p>

  <h2>Delete your Creators Club account</h2>
  <p>In the mobile app, delete your account from your account settings. After the grace period your account and its data are erased, except records the law requires us to keep, such as invoices.</p>

  <h2>Ask us</h2>
  <p>Send a request through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a> with the subject “Data deletion request”. If you only interacted with an account that uses Creators Club (for example, you commented on a creator’s post), include your Instagram or YouTube username and the creator’s username. We reply within 30 days.</p>
</LegalLayout>
